reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:29:40-07:00","id":917341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=917314#post917314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... they will never stop rampaging, they will heal with rage</div> </div> </div> </div>That only works once per scene, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they will heal with blood, they will suck everything that tries to stop them dry, they will hunt down all leeches in the city and SUCK EM DRY before trying to suck up the rest of the town. They are more dangerous than Samuel Height on a short term... possibly not so much long term. </div> </div> </div>On a long term, the existence of all Haights drops to ashtray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:12:16-07:00","id":917359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=917312#post917312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to save time, &quot;What about [Thing that combines any two or more major splat templates] is it possible how would it work?&quot;<br /> Answer, &quot;It ends badly for everyone, do you not remember Samuel Height?&quot;<br /> <br /> :P</div> </div> </div> </div>One case that's actually turned out to be somewhat beneficial: the Silent Strider Wepauwet, who combines Garou and Arisen. He found out he could only resurrect once; if he died again, he'd end up cursed to wander the Umbra as a spirit, denied access to his living people or the tribal homeland. However, his unique nature allows him to bypass part of Sutekh's curse on the Striders, serving as an intermediary between the tribe and their ancestor-spirits, and he's found a way to grant a select few Strider cubs access to their ancestors as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:32:39-07:00","id":917396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=917314#post917314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> they will heal with rage, they will heal with blood</div> </div> </div> </div>Storyteller's guide on page 198 states &quot;Abominations cannot regenerate their wounds as do Garou; Abominations may heal themselves only by spending blood&quot;. So Rage healing once a scene is out even there. The newest V20 rules from Black Hand aren't much better since I'm not sure if they are intended to be vampire only splat translations (burn blood to shapeshift or side step, no mention of Rage or any other form of healing, also in this book Abominations are not allowed to have any in clan disciplines. In V20 they got a lot more flaws to boot). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:50:50-07:00","id":917431,"title":"","content":"Okay assuming it was Possible. How would I go about making this NPC?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Don't shoot that man he's an unpaid intern.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7070-sakkhet","name":"Sakkhet","avatar":"https://forum.theony