 the Nonelysium<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:14:09-07:00","id":919855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=919523#post919523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The solution to many of the larps I've been for Elysium blowing up have been &quot;Don't declare places we gather Elysium&quot;. I've often found this to be a hilarious display of weakness for both the Prince and the Keeper of the Nonelysium</div> </div> </div> </div>H.C. Durand was the only Gangrel in Chicago after the Clan left the Camarilla, so the Prince him Master of Elysium as consolation prize. The best moment was when the Ventrue Justicar's pet Ghouled Dhampyric Mage filled <i>my</i> nightclub with sand. The GMs forced me to make a Frenzy Test every step he took as he descended toward the bleeding unconscious fuckwit. My character kicked him in the nuts, then told the staff to order pool toys, beach umbrellas, and extra rum for the coming week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:04:53-07:00","id":925518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=917836#post917836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a>, you mean like Kitsune (Take that wood be sire: You just bit a pillar of cleansing fire!) Nuwisha (Nope, nothing happens) and Ananasi (Nope, nothing happens) and Mokol\u00e9 (A Dragon Rampage &amp; Detonation at dawn please, extra sized) or Corax (Gain a goon, but blow it up at dawn) Nagah (Nothing happens, again)? No, You MUST mean Ratkin Liam: Rotting Rat Abominations, which walk till they are nothing but Skeletons - even over the point they lack any brain, Because standard Abominations like Garou, Ajaba, Gurahl and Bastet (who autoloose gnosis all 28 Days (later)) are no fun clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I seem to remember something about a 4th generation Setite Mokole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpa