ame":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:34:27-07:00","id":925582,"title":"","content":"Agreed, and it'd be a useful tool for Setites. Imagine being a Clutch and hearing about this supposed bastard of Set, an actual Mokole-Vampire who survived more then just the first night. It'd be your holy duty to end it (great trap to Set....all puns intended).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:55:44-07:00","id":926319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=925534#post925534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a mention in a vampire book with no write up. So it can go 1 of two ways, its either a lie (come on they are Setites) or you can go all Deus ex Antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably just a shapeshifting variant of Serpentis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:24:59-07:00","id":926428,"title":"","content":"A buddy of mine told me about a serpentis power called &quot;Apep Semblance&quot;, where the Setite turned all Azhi Dahaka...issue is I haven't been able to find this power anywhere. If anyone knows where this power can be found, I'd be interested in knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T02:59:00-07:00","id":929140,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sobek_(Abomination\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sobek_(Abomination</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T08:58:37-07:00","id":929240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=929140#post929140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sobek_(Abomination\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sobek_(Abomination</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know who he is, and like this website says &quot;if&quot;, the site itself isn't even certain on what Sobek is, and mentions typically it can't happen and reference that Helios is very powerful. So the big question is, what do you run in your game? I'm personally fond of it being a bet Setite lie (mostly because I grew tired of &quot;this is the rule every time EXCEPT THAT ONE AWESOME TIME THE DEVELOPERS WANTED TO MAKE A SPECIAL OMG NPC!!!&quot;). If others want an embraced Mokole they can. Vampire and Werewolf developers back in the day weren't exactly great at talking to one another, and Vampire was big on snagging some of Werewolf's stuff (this Sobek abom, the Revanent family who were all Shadow Lord kin and could learn Shadow Lord gifts, 1st ed Gangrel clan book saying that Gangrel can learn werewolf rites, ect.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:40:08-07:00","id":930279,"title":"","content":"I think it's kinda the same territory as the discussion on who or what Odin/Wotan/AllFather actually was and what was his role, and how many variants of him were around. The books quite contradict each other left and right. As this is the Werewolf forum and the Setites are just a special type of baddies there, I'd go with the Mokole interpretation being the right one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:17:52-07:00","id":930895,"title":"","content":"To be fair, in Werewolf cosmology, Set is special even among Vampires, as he's the one who cursed an entire tribe of Werewolves and forced them to leave their homeland forever, cut them off from their ancestors, removed their ability to travel to their Umbral homeland, etc. If someone said that Set had capability to break Helios' blessing like that, I wouldn't bat an eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-13-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:32:56-07:00","id":930926,"title":"","content":"It's why I called it Deuce ex Antedeluvian. Ist just not something I'm really big on personally. However Sobek is 1 time and even the book only says rumor, so it's why I side with the mokol\u00e8 breed book and the W20 CB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-13-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T18:36:43-07:00","id":931120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=930895#post930895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, in Werewolf cosmology, Set is special even among Vampires, as he's the one who cursed an entire tribe of Werewolves and forced them to leave their homeland forever, cut them off from their ancestors, removed their ability to travel to their Umbral homeland, etc. If someone said that Set had capability to break Helios' blessing like that, I wouldn't bat an eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was presented as some kind of Ren Hekau-esque BS involving true names and the ancestors of the Striders. It was a very specific blow that hasn't been replicated and might have simply been a one-off, rather than something within easy reach..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T04:32:59-07:00","id":931271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/917270-rokea-abominations?p=930895#post930895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, in Werewolf cosmology, Set is special even among Vampires, as he's the one who cursed an entire tribe of Werewolves and forced them to leave their homeland forever, cut them off from their ancestors, removed their ability to travel to their Umbral homeland, etc. If someone said that Set had capability to break Helios' blessing like that, I wouldn't bat an eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Set cursed the tribe to never rest in their homeland, true, but the pride and folly of the tribal elders were responsible for the loss of the Umbral homeland and their ancestor spirits. (W20 Umbra p. 90)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}